I've been at the game for about two years now, & finally ascended
(apologies for having forgotten to cut/paste final stats &c--I was so
exhilarated I didn't even think!).

Game got off to a good start, quaffing from a fountain on lvl 1 or 2
and unleashing a peaceful water demon--blessed +3 gdsm. Since I was
lawful, I got excalibur early. Coaligned temple in Minetown--Tyr
rewarded my sacs with Mojo, Fire Brand, and then Frost Brand. Not too
much out of the ordinary--amulet of reflection from Sobokan, found
speed boots in the castle, blessed bag of holding from WoW...in fact, I
was so lucky in finding items, I never used my third wish from the
wand.

Oh, yes--and I was really lucky that an early amulet of life saving
saved me from my own stupidity on the quest--fell into a pit with a
cockatrice corpse.

It got a bit exciting in Orcus-town when Orcus summoned Yeenoghu--I
wasn't dying yet, but they Yeenoghu had me constantly confused and they
were slowly but surely sapping my HP--until they backed me into a
corner with a cockatrice.

Also got a little touch-and-go on the plane of Water--Rodney stole the
Amulet, I immediately killed him, and then the bubble moved away--I
thought for a while that the thing was permenantly lost below the
waves. Thought of wishing for an amulet of magical breathing, so I
could walk along the bottom searching (would that have worked?)--but
I'd taken out my wand of wishing earlier (in case the bag got cursed)
and someone zapped me with a lightning wand--eventually found Rodney's
corpse, nearly in despair, a couple of steps before I wandered onto the
portal.

Anyhow...finally made it. I think I have some major RNG karma to pay
back.



